assistant: Subject: Read unit_amount when vendor omits price

Root cause: vendor API version 2026-10-01 renamed the product's `price` field to `unit_amount`. The value is still in dollars: p-1001 is 1199 in both the v1 fixture and the recorded call. `get_product` only read `p.price ?? null`, so on the new version it returned `price: null` even though a price was in the response. The fix adds an optional `unit_amount` to the `VendorProduct` type in `src/tools/get_product.ts` and maps `price: p.price ?? p.unit_amount ?? null`. v1 responses still use `price`, so their output is unchanged. typecheck, lint and test all pass (13 tests), though none of the fixtures covers the new vendor version. `search_products` also reads only `p.price`, so it may break the same way on the new version. I left it alone because nothing shows what its new response looks like.

